@host = https://localhost:7210

# Paste a Frontegg-issued access token (Authorization: Bearer) and/or a Frontegg API key (X-API-KEY).
# Both are live credentials — keep them out of commits.
@accessToken =
@apiKey =

### Anonymous. The only endpoint carrying AllowAnonymous, so the only one that answers without a credential.
GET {{host}}/api/ping

### No credential on a gated endpoint -> 401 from the package's gating middleware, before authorization runs.
GET {{host}}/api/reports

### Bearer access token.
GET {{host}}/api/diagnostics/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### API key. Same endpoint, different handler: lifetime is not validated, revocation is checked per request.
GET {{host}}/api/diagnostics/me
X-API-KEY: {{apiKey}}

### Every claim on the principal, minus the token claims. Start here when a field on /me is empty.
GET {{host}}/api/diagnostics/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Evaluate a permission policy without being gated by it — 200 either way, `granted` carries the answer.
GET {{host}}/api/diagnostics/permission?key=sample.reports.read
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Same for the numeric form. `mapsToKey` is null when FronteggSettings:PermissionIdMappings has no entry,
### which is the most common reason a permid: gate denies unexpectedly.
GET {{host}}/api/diagnostics/permission-id/101
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Pre-flight the client-credentials tenant token. Reports success only; the token is never returned.
GET {{host}}/api/diagnostics/tenant-token
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Gated on perm:sample.reports.read.
GET {{host}}/api/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Gated on permid:101.
DELETE {{host}}/api/reports/7
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Gated on the admin role rather than a permission.
GET {{host}}/api/reports/admin-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
